IMPORT prelude

-- A New Tax System (Family Assistance) (Administration) Act 1999 (Cth) -- how a parent claims family tax benefit, how it is
-- paid on an income estimate, what is reconciled after the income year and when, what happens when the estimate was too
-- low or too high (debts, top-ups, the supplements), and the parent's rights of review: the need for a claim and the kinds
-- of claim (ss 5, 7, 7A, 8, 9, 10, 14A, 15, 15A, 15B; s 3 "early claim day"); payment by instalment on an estimate (ss 20,
-- 23, 31A(2), 31E); the FTB reconciliation conditions and the supplements held back until they are met (ss 32A-32D, 32J,
-- 32P, 105A); the indexed estimate and indexed actual income (ss 20A(5), 20B(2), (4)); loss of FTB for an unlodged tax
-- return (ss 28(1)-(2), 28AA); the estimate bar after two nil years (s 32AF, with the exceptions in ss 32AI-32AL as facts);
-- debts and their recovery (ss 71, 77, 78, 78C, 78D, 93B, 97, 99, 100(4)-(6)); and review (ss 108(3), 109D, 109E, 111A).
--
-- SEAT: the parent (the claimant) -- "How do I claim, what is reconciled at year end, and what if I was overpaid?". Every
-- decision is phrased as the parent asks it: "Must I make a claim to be paid this?", "Is my claim for FTB by instalment
-- effective?", "By the end of which income year must I claim FTB for a past period?", "Have I satisfied the FTB
-- reconciliation conditions?", "What is the result of reconciling my FTB for the year?", "When is my debt due?", "Must I
-- pay interest charge?", "By when must I apply for review?". Where the Act hands a judgment to the Secretary (an estimate
-- is "reasonable", s 20(1)(d); "special circumstances", ss 10(2)(b)(ii), 32C(3)(b); a further period allowed; an exemption
-- from the bank account or TFN requirement), it is asked as a fact the parent can state (the Secretary has decided so).
--
-- Provisions covered: s 3 ("early claim day", "estimated income basis"), s 5, s 7(1)-(3), s 7A(2), (4), s 8(2), (7), s 9,
-- s 10(1)(a), (b), (2), (2A), (3), s 14A(1), (2), (4), s 15A, s 15B, s 20(1), (2), (2A), s 20A(5), s 20B(2), (4), s 23(1),
-- (2), s 28(1), (2), s 28AA(1),
-- s 31A(2), s 31E(2), (3), s 32A(2), s 32B, s 32C, s 32D (couple throughout, no separation), s 32J, s 32P, s 32AF(1)-(2)
-- with ss 32AI, 32AJ, 32AK, 32AL as facts, s 71(1), (2), s 77(2), s 78(1), s 78C(1), s 78D(1), s 93B, s 97(1)-(3), s 99(1),
-- s 100(4)-(6),
-- s 105A(2), s 108(3), s 109D(1), (3), (6), s 109E(1), (2AA), (2A), s 111A(1), (5).
--
-- Edition: compilation register id C2026C00426 (two volumes), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00491.txt (retrieved 13 October 2026). No instrument is deposited and the plan names
-- none. Three figures come from elsewhere and are inputs: the small-debt amount (s 99 refers to s 1237AAA of the Social
-- Security Act 1991; the note says "Immediately before 1 July 2026, the amount was $250"), the base interest rate (s 78C:
-- the RBA 90-day bank bill yield), and the 7-day instalment class (s 23(3A), a Minister's instrument, asked as a fact). The
-- dollar amounts of family tax benefit come from the Family Assistance Act baseline (fa-families.l4, rates as printed) and
-- are inputs here. The formulas the text deposit lost (ss 20A(5), 20B(4), 100(6)) are transcribed by hand from the
-- authorised Word rendering of the same compilation (volume 1) in ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00491.formulas.md
-- (2026-10-21) and encoded below. The AWE figures and the Minister's interest rate they need are inputs.
--
-- INCOME YEARS are written as the calendar year in which they END: 2036 is the income year 1 July 2035 to 30 June 2036.
-- Days are counted from a stated day (the claim, the notice), as the provisions count them.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: approved care organisations; bereavement claims (ss 11, 18, 32-33 FA Act); FTB advances (Part 3 Div 2); the
-- TFN and bank account variations (ss 26-27A) beyond the claim stage; ss 28(3)-(6) (restoring FTB after late lodgment) and
-- the prohibited periods of ss 32AA-32AE; ss 28B-30B (other variations); s 31 (change of circumstances) beyond the s 31A
-- revised estimate; when the Secretary may give an indexation notice and its start day (ss 20A(1)-(4), 20B(1), (3)) and s
-- 20C (couples); maintenance income (ss 31B, 32N); ss 32E, 32F (a couple separating in
-- the next income year), 32M (foreign income, tax free pensions), 32Q; the exceptions in ss 32AG, 32AH, 32AM; the child care
-- subsidy (Part 3A, ss 103-103C, 105C-105E) and the stillborn baby payment and single income family supplement; recovery
-- by garnishee, set-off and court (ss 80-93A) beyond the fact of no time limit; waiver under ss 98, 100(1)-(3), 101, 102 and write-off
-- (s 95); Secretary-initiated review (ss 104-107) beyond s 105A; ART procedure (ss 112-141); offences (s 25, Part 6); the
-- whole of Parts 7-9.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `A New Tax System (Family Assistance) (Administration) Act 1999`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the positive part of` MEANS
    IF `x` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `x` ELSE 0

§§ `5, 7 -- must I claim, and what kind of claim`

-- s 5(1): "The only way that a person can become entitled to be paid family tax benefit is to make a claim in accordance
-- with this Subdivision." (2) "A claim is not required for an amount of family tax benefit under section 58AA of the Family
-- Assistance Act" (the newborn upfront payment). s 7(1): a claim may be "(a) for payment of family tax benefit by
-- instalment; or (b) for payment of family tax benefit for a past period; or (c) ... by single payment/in substitution
-- because of the death of another individual". Gloss: "by instalment" is fortnightly payment from now on; "for a past
-- period" is one lump sum for days already gone (the lump-sum claim).
DECLARE `What I want to be paid` IS ONE OF
    `FTB by instalment`
    `FTB for a past period`
    `FTB because of the death of another person`
    `the newborn upfront payment`

@export Must I make a claim to be paid this (s 5)?
GIVEN `the payment` IS A `What I want to be paid` @desc What you want to be paid
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I make a claim to be paid this` IF
    NOT (`the payment` EQUALS `the newborn upfront payment`)

§§ `7, 7A, 8, 9, s 3 "early claim day" -- is my claim for FTB by instalment effective`

-- s 7(2): to be effective a claim must be made in the form and manner, with the information and documents, the Secretary
-- requires; (aa) for an instalment claim "the bank account requirement set out in section 7A must be satisfied"; (b) "the tax
-- file number requirement in section 8". s 7A(2): the claimant provides "(a) details of a bank account ... or (b) a
-- statement that the claimant will nominate ... such a bank account within 28 days after the claim is made"; (4) the
-- Secretary may exempt. s 8(2): a statement of a TFN (or that one is unknown and asked for, or applied for) "must be made in
-- relation to each TFN claim person" -- for an instalment claim the claimant and any partner at the time (s 3); (7) the
-- Secretary may exempt a partner whose TFN the claimant cannot obtain.
-- s 7(3): "A claim is not effective if it is made before the early claim day." s 3: the early claim day "means the day
-- occurring 97 days before the day that, on the day the claim is made, is the expected day on which the child ... will
-- become an FTB child of the claimant". So a parent can claim up to 97 days before the expected birth.
-- s 9: not effective if (a) an earlier instalment claim is undetermined, (b) "the claimant is already entitled to be paid
-- family tax benefit by instalment", or (c) a nil variation for failing a requirement (ss 27-30B) still bars a new claim.
DECLARE `My instalment claim` HAS
    `made in the form and manner the Secretary requires`          IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 7(2)(a)
    `I gave bank account details or said I would within 28 days` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 7A(2)
    `the Secretary exempted me from the bank account requirement` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 7A(4)
    `a TFN statement is made for me`                              IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 8(2), (3)-(5)
    `a TFN statement is made for my partner, or I have no partner` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 8(2)
    `the Secretary exempted my partner from the TFN requirement`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 8(7)
    `days before the expected day my child becomes my FTB child`  IS A NUMBER   -- s 3, s 7(3); 0 if already
    `an earlier instalment claim of mine is undetermined`         IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 9(a)
    `I am already entitled to FTB by instalment`                  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 9(b)
    `a nil variation under ss 27-30B still bars me`               IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 9(c)

`the early claim window in days` MEANS 97

@export Is my claim for FTB by instalment effective (ss 7, 7A, 8, 9)?
GIVEN `my claim` IS A `My instalment claim` @desc Your claim, its bank and TFN details, and how early it was made
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim for FTB by instalment effective` IF
        `my claim`'s `made in the form and manner the Secretary requires`
    AND (    `my claim`'s `I gave bank account details or said I would within 28 days`
         OR  `my claim`'s `the Secretary exempted me from the bank account requirement`)
    AND `my claim`'s `a TFN statement is made for me`
    AND (    `my claim`'s `a TFN statement is made for my partner, or I have no partner`
         OR  `my claim`'s `the Secretary exempted my partner from the TFN requirement`)
    AND `my claim`'s `days before the expected day my child becomes my FTB child` AT MOST `the early claim window in days`
    AND (NOT `my claim`'s `an earlier instalment claim of mine is undetermined`)
    AND (NOT `my claim`'s `I am already entitled to FTB by instalment`)
    AND (NOT `my claim`'s `a nil variation under ss 27-30B still bars me`)

-- s 15A(1): if the claimant said a bank account would be nominated later, the claim can be determined only if "within 28
-- days after the claim is made, the person nominates, and provides details of, a bank account"; (2) otherwise "the claim is
-- taken never to have been made". Nominating ON day 28 is treated as within time (INFERENCE: "within 28 days after").
@export Is my claim taken never to have been made because I did not give my bank account in time (s 15A)?
GIVEN `I said I would nominate an account later` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim said you would give bank account details later
      `I have nominated an account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since nominated an account
      `days after the claim when I nominated it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the claim you nominated it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim lost for want of bank details` IF
        `I said I would nominate an account later`
    AND NOT (`I have nominated an account` AND `days after the claim when I nominated it` AT MOST 28)

-- s 15B: a claim made before the child is an FTB child, where the claimant would likely be eligible, must not be determined
-- "until the earlier of ... (c) the time when the child becomes an FTB child of the claimant, or is stillborn; (d) 28 days
-- after the day that, on the day the claim is made, is the expected day". Counted in days from the claim.
@export How many days after my early claim will it be determined, at the latest (s 15B)?
GIVEN `days from my claim to the expected day` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after your claim the child was expected to become your FTB child (usually the due date)
      `days from my claim to the day my child became my FTB child` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after your claim the child actually became your FTB child (or was stillborn)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many days until my early claim is determined` MEANS
    min `days from my claim to the day my child became my FTB child` (`days from my claim to the expected day` PLUS 28)

§§ `10, 14A -- my lump-sum claim for a past period`

-- s 10(2): a past-period claim "is not effective if: (a) the period does not fall wholly within one income year; or (b) ...
-- the claim is made after the end of: (i) the first income year after the relevant income year; or (ii) such further period
-- (if any) as the Secretary allows, if the Secretary is satisfied that there are special circumstances". (2A) "The further
-- period ... must end no later than the end of the second income year after the relevant income year." The same pattern
-- sets the tax return deadline in ss 14A(2), (4) and 32C(3)-(4). Income years are named by the year they end.
@export By the end of which income year must I act (claim, lodge or notify) for an income year (ss 10(2), (2A), 14A, 32C)?
GIVEN `the income year` IS A NUMBER @desc The income year concerned (named by the year it ends: 2036 for 2035-36)
      `the Secretary allowed a further period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary, satisfied of special circumstances, allowed you more time
      `the income year the further period ends in` IS A NUMBER @desc The income year in which that further period ends
GIVETH A NUMBER
`By the end of which income year must I act` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary allowed a further period`
    THEN min `the income year the further period ends in` (`the income year` PLUS 2)
    ELSE `the income year` PLUS 1

-- s 10(1): not effective if "(a) the claimant has previously made a claim ... for any of the past period" or "(b) the
-- claimant was entitled to be paid family tax benefit by instalment at any time in the past period". (3): a claim for a
-- period in the current income year by someone now eligible and free to claim instalments must be "accompanied by a claim
-- for payment of family tax benefit by instalment". The TFN requirement (s 7(2)(b)) applies to a past-period claim too.
DECLARE `My past-period claim` HAS
    `made in the form and manner the Secretary requires`   IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 7(2)(a)
    `TFN statements are made as s 8 requires`              IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 7(2)(b), s 8
    `the period falls wholly within one income year`       IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10(2)(a)
    `the income year of the period`                        IS A NUMBER   -- s 10(2)(b)
    `the income year I claim in`                           IS A NUMBER   -- s 10(2)(b)
    `the Secretary allowed a further period`               IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10(2)(b)(ii)
    `the income year the further period ends in`           IS A NUMBER   -- s 10(2A)
    `I already claimed for some of the period`             IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10(1)(a)
    `I was paid by instalment at some time in the period`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 10(1)(b)
    `s 10(3) requires an instalment claim that I did not make` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 10(3)

@export Is my claim for FTB for a past period effective (ss 7, 10)?
GIVEN `my claim` IS A `My past-period claim` @desc Your lump-sum claim: the period, when you claim, and any earlier claims or instalments
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim for FTB for a past period effective` IF
        `my claim`'s `made in the form and manner the Secretary requires`
    AND `my claim`'s `TFN statements are made as s 8 requires`
    AND `my claim`'s `the period falls wholly within one income year`
    AND `my claim`'s `the income year I claim in` AT MOST
            `By the end of which income year must I act` (`my claim`'s `the income year of the period`)
                                                        (`my claim`'s `the Secretary allowed a further period`)
                                                        (`my claim`'s `the income year the further period ends in`)
    AND (NOT `my claim`'s `I already claimed for some of the period`)
    AND (NOT `my claim`'s `I was paid by instalment at some time in the period`)
    AND (NOT `my claim`'s `s 10(3) requires an instalment claim that I did not make`)

-- s 14A(1): a past-period claim for one of "the 2 income years before the one in which the claim is made" is "taken never
-- to have been made" if (2) the claimant "is required to lodge an income tax return for the past period income year" and
-- "has not lodged the return before the end of: (i) the first income year after the past period income year; or (ii) such
-- further period" (no later than the second, (4)). The partner limb (3) and the no-return limb (3A) are not encoded.
-- "Lodged in" year 0 means not lodged.
@export Is my lump-sum claim taken never to have been made because my tax return was late (s 14A)?
GIVEN `the income year of the period` IS A NUMBER @desc The income year your claim is for
      `the income year I claim in` IS A NUMBER @desc The income year in which you claim
      `I must lodge a tax return for that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are required to lodge an income tax return for that year
      `the income year I lodged it in` IS A NUMBER @desc The income year in which you lodged that return (0 if not lodged)
      `the Secretary allowed a further period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary allowed more time for special circumstances
      `the income year the further period ends in` IS A NUMBER @desc The income year in which that further period ends
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my lump-sum claim lost for a late tax return` IF
        `the income year of the period` LESS THAN `the income year I claim in`
    AND `the income year of the period` AT LEAST `the income year I claim in` MINUS 2
    AND `I must lodge a tax return for that year`
    AND (   `the income year I lodged it in` EQUALS 0
         OR `the income year I lodged it in` GREATER THAN `deadline`)
    WHERE
        `deadline` MEANS `By the end of which income year must I act` `the income year of the period`
                                                                     `the Secretary allowed a further period`
                                                                     `the income year the further period ends in`

§§ `20, 23 -- how I am paid by instalment on my income estimate`

-- s 20(1): where adjusted taxable income "is not available (for example, because the taxable income ... cannot be known until
-- after the end of the relevant income year)" and the individual "gives the Secretary an estimate" which "the Secretary
-- considers ... to be reasonable", and no indexed-estimate notice (ss 20A, 20B) has a start day that has passed, "the
-- Secretary may determine the individual's eligibility for, or rate of, family tax benefit on the basis of the estimate".
-- (2): if the estimate is not considered reasonable, "the eligibility or rate cannot be determined" and s 19 applies (no
-- entitlement). (2A): after a notice's start day, with no reasonable estimate since, the indexed estimate or indexed actual
-- income in the notice is used. s 3: either way FTB is "worked out on an estimated income basis".
DECLARE `What my FTB rate is worked out on` IS ONE OF
    `my own estimate`
    `the indexed figure in the Secretary's notice`
    `nothing: I am not entitled while my estimate is not reasonable`

@export What is my FTB by instalment worked out on (s 20)?
GIVEN `I gave an estimate since the last notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given an estimate of your adjusted taxable income since any indexation notice
      `the Secretary considers my estimate reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary considers that estimate reasonable
      `a notice's start day has passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an indexed estimate or indexed actual income notice has been given to you with a start day that has arrived
GIVETH A `What my FTB rate is worked out on`
`What is my FTB worked out on` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `I gave an estimate since the last notice` AND `the Secretary considers my estimate reasonable` THEN `my own estimate`
           IF `I gave an estimate since the last notice`                                                     THEN `nothing: I am not entitled while my estimate is not reasonable`
           IF `a notice's start day has passed`                                                              THEN `the indexed figure in the Secretary's notice`
           OTHERWISE `nothing: I am not entitled while my estimate is not reasonable`

-- s 20A(5): "Calculate an indexed estimate (which may be nil) for the individual by multiplying the individual's current ATI
-- number ... by the indexation factor, rounding the result to the nearest dollar and rounding 50 cents upwards. The
-- indexation factor is the greater of 1 and the factor worked out to 3 decimal places as follows (increasing the factor by
-- 0.001 if it would, if worked out to 4 decimal places, end in a number greater than 4):" -- transcribed
-- (C2004A00491.formulas.md):
--     AWE for the reference period in the most recent November / AWE for the reference period in the highest previous November
-- s 20B(4) uses the same factor on the actual income that became known to the Secretary. "AWE" is the Australian
-- Statistician's Average Weekly Earnings figure; "most recent November" is the November of the income year before the one
-- the start day falls in; "highest previous November" the November (from 2004) with the highest AWE before it. The AWE
-- figures are published numbers: inputs. "Worked out to 3 decimal places" is read as cutting off after the third place,
-- so that the 0.001 increase completes a round-half-up (an INFERENCE about "worked out to").
GIVEN `AWE in the most recent November` IS A NUMBER
      `AWE in the highest previous November` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the indexation factor` MEANS
    max 1 (IF `fourth place` GREATER THAN 4 THEN `three places` PLUS 0.001 ELSE `three places`)
    WHERE
        `ratio`        MEANS `AWE in the most recent November` DIVIDED BY `AWE in the highest previous November`
        `three places` MEANS FLOOR (`ratio` TIMES 1000) DIVIDED BY 1000
        `fourth place` MEANS FLOOR (`ratio` TIMES 10000) MINUS (FLOOR (`ratio` TIMES 1000) TIMES 10)

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`to the nearest dollar, 50 cents up` MEANS FLOOR (`x` PLUS 0.5)

@export What is my indexed estimate (s 20A(5))?
GIVEN `my current ATI number` IS A NUMBER @desc The income the Secretary is permitted to use for you under s 20 (or an indexed actual income in a notice whose start day has not arrived), s 20A(6)
      `AWE in the most recent November` IS A NUMBER @desc Average Weekly Earnings for the reference period in the most recent November
      `AWE in the highest previous November` IS A NUMBER @desc Average Weekly Earnings for the reference period in the highest previous November
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my indexed estimate` MEANS
    `to the nearest dollar, 50 cents up`
        (`my current ATI number` TIMES (`the indexation factor` `AWE in the most recent November` `AWE in the highest previous November`))

@export What is my indexed actual income (s 20B(4))?
GIVEN `my actual income for the latest known year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your adjusted taxable income for the most recent income year the Secretary knows it for
      `AWE in the most recent November` IS A NUMBER @desc Average Weekly Earnings for the reference period in the most recent November
      `AWE in the highest previous November` IS A NUMBER @desc Average Weekly Earnings for the reference period in the highest previous November
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my indexed actual income` MEANS
    `to the nearest dollar, 50 cents up`
        (`my actual income for the latest known year` TIMES (`the indexation factor` `AWE in the most recent November` `AWE in the highest previous November`))

-- s 20B(2): the Secretary may give an indexed actual income notice only if "(b) the indexed actual income is greater than the
-- individual's current ATI number". The other conditions (s 20B(1)) are facts.
@export Can I be given a notice that my FTB will be worked out on an indexed actual income (s 20B(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the s 20B(1) conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are paid FTB by instalment on an indexed figure, have given no reasonable estimate since the last notice, and a later year's actual income has become known
      `my indexed actual income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your indexed actual income (see the question above)
      `my current ATI number` IS A NUMBER @desc Your current ATI number (s 20B(5))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be given an indexed actual income notice` IF
    `the s 20B(1) conditions are met` AND `my indexed actual income` GREATER THAN `my current ATI number`

-- s 23(1): "the Secretary must, after each instalment period ..., pay the instalment amount to the claimant ... to the
-- credit of a bank account nominated and maintained by the claimant". (2) "instalment amount means the amount accruing for
-- the days in the instalment period for which an entitlement ... arose"; "instalment period means ... (a) the period of 14
-- days ..." or (b) 7 days for a claimant in a class specified by the Minister (s 23(3A)) and determined by the Secretary (s
-- 23(3B)). The daily rate is the rate in the determination (s 16(2)); how it is derived from the annual rate is in the
-- Family Assistance Act and is an input here.
@export How many days are in each of my FTB instalment periods (s 23(2))?
GIVEN `the Secretary has determined I have 7-day instalment periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary has determined under s 23(3B) that you are paid weekly
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many days are in my instalment period` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary has determined I have 7-day instalment periods` THEN 7 ELSE 14

@export How much is my FTB instalment (s 23(2))?
GIVEN `my daily rate` IS A NUMBER @desc Your daily rate of FTB under the determination
      `days of entitlement in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of the instalment period you were entitled
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my FTB instalment` MEANS `my daily rate` TIMES `days of entitlement in the period`

§§ `31A(2), 31E -- when I revise my estimate during the year`

-- s 31A(1): if the claimant gives a revised estimate the Secretary considers reasonable, the determination must be varied to
-- use it. (2) the variation has effect: "(a) if it results in an increase ...: (i) ... from the day on which the revised
-- estimate was provided ...; or (ii) if the first day of the income year to which the revised estimate relates occurs after
-- [that day]--from that first day"; "(b) if it results in a decrease ...: ... (iii) if the day after the end of the last
-- instalment period before the variation takes place occurs after the days identified in subparagraphs (i) and (ii)--from
-- the day first-mentioned in this subparagraph". So an increase can start the day the estimate is given; a decrease never
-- reaches back into an instalment period already paid. Days are counted from any fixed day.
@export From which day does my revised income estimate change my FTB rate (s 31A(2))?
GIVEN `my rate goes up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the revised estimate increases your rate (FALSE if it decreases it)
      `the day I gave the revised estimate` IS A NUMBER @desc The day you gave the revised estimate
      `the first day of the income year it relates to` IS A NUMBER @desc The first day of the income year the estimate is for
      `the day after my last paid instalment period` IS A NUMBER @desc The day after the end of the last instalment period before the variation
GIVETH A NUMBER
`From which day does my revised estimate take effect` MEANS
    IF `my rate goes up`
    THEN max `the day I gave the revised estimate` `the first day of the income year it relates to`
    ELSE max (max `the day I gave the revised estimate` `the first day of the income year it relates to`)
             `the day after my last paid instalment period`

-- s 31E(2) method statement: "Step 1. Work out the total amount ... the claimant is or was entitled to be paid during the
-- period beginning at the start of the income year and ending at the end of the day before the applicable day. Step 2. ...
-- would have been entitled ... using ... the revised estimate ... Step 3. Take the amount worked out at step 2 away from
-- the amount worked out at step 1. Step 4. If ... greater than zero, work out the number of days ... beginning on the
-- applicable day and ending at the end of the last day in the income year. Step 5. ... dividing the amount worked out at
-- step 3 by the number of days ..., and rounding ... to the nearest cent". (3) the daily rate for the rest of the year "is
-- reduced (but not below nil) by that daily overpayment rate". This is how an over-paid part of the year is clawed back
-- inside the year, before reconciliation. Rounding to the cent is not encoded (the cases divide exactly).
@export What is my daily overpayment rate after I revise my estimate (s 31E(2))?
GIVEN `what I was paid so far this year` IS A NUMBER @desc FTB you were entitled to from 1 July to the day before the change (step 1)
      `what I would have been paid on the new estimate` IS A NUMBER @desc FTB for the same days worked out on the revised estimate (step 2)
      `days left in the income year` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the applicable day to 30 June inclusive (step 4)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my daily overpayment rate` MEANS
    IF `step 3` GREATER THAN 0 AND `days left in the income year` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `step 3` DIVIDED BY `days left in the income year`
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `step 3` MEANS `what I was paid so far this year` MINUS `what I would have been paid on the new estimate`

@export What is my daily FTB rate for the rest of the year after the clawback (s 31E(3))?
GIVEN `my new daily rate` IS A NUMBER @desc Your daily rate on the revised estimate
      `my daily overpayment rate` IS A NUMBER @desc Your daily overpayment rate (above)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my daily rate for the rest of the year` MEANS
    `the positive part of` (`my new daily rate` MINUS `my daily overpayment rate`)

§§ `32A-32P, 105A -- the FTB reconciliation conditions`

-- s 32A(2): in making or varying an instalment or past-period determination "the Secretary must disregard" the FTB Part A
-- supplement (Sch 1 cl 3 step 1(ca), cl 25 step 1(d), cl 38A(1)) and the FTB Part B supplement (cl 29(1)(b), 29(2) step
-- 1(b), 31A(1)) "unless and until ... the first individual has satisfied the FTB reconciliation conditions". s 105A(2): once
-- they are satisfied the Secretary "must" review the determination and "take account of" the supplements.
-- s 32B: the conditions are satisfied at the relevant reconciliation time under each of ss 32C-32Q that applies (the latest).
-- s 32C: applies if the individual "is or was required to lodge an income tax return for the relevant income year" and cl
-- 38L (income support) "did not apply ... at any time" (that limb disregarded for a member of a couple, (2)); the time is
-- "when an assessment is made ... so long as the ... return ... was lodged before the end of: (a) the first income year
-- after the relevant income year; or (b) such further period" (no later than the second, (4)).
-- s 32D: a member of a couple "throughout that period" whose partner must lodge, still a couple at the end of the next
-- income year: the time is the assessment of the partner, lodged in the same time. (ss 32E, 32F, separation, not encoded.)
-- s 32J: where the individual or anyone whose income counts "is not required to lodge": the earlier of the individual
-- notifying the adjusted taxable income in the same time, or the Secretary being satisfied it can be worked out.
-- s 32P: single throughout, cl 38L throughout (income support), no maintenance income: "the end of the relevant income year".
DECLARE `My year` HAS
    `I must lodge a tax return for the year`                        IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 32C(1)(a)
    `I was on income support at some time in the period`            IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 32C(1)(b): cl 38L
    `I was on income support throughout the period`                 IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 32P(1)(b)
    `I was a member of a couple throughout the period`              IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 32D(1)(a)
    `I was a member of a couple at some time in the period`         IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 32C(2), 32P(1)(a)
    `I had maintenance income`                                      IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 32P(1)(c)
    `I lodged my return in time`                                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 32C(3): by the s 10(2)-pattern deadline
    `my assessment has been made`                                   IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 32C(3)
    `my partner must lodge a tax return for the year`               IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 32D(1)(b)
    `my partner lodged in time`                                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 32D(2)
    `my partner's assessment has been made`                         IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 32D(2)
    `someone whose income counts need not lodge`                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 32J(1)
    `I notified my income in time, or the Secretary can work it out` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 32J(2)
    `the income year has ended`                                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 32P(2)

GIVEN `y` IS A `My year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 32C applies` IF
        `y`'s `I must lodge a tax return for the year`
    AND (   (NOT `y`'s `I was on income support at some time in the period`)
         OR `y`'s `I was a member of a couple at some time in the period`)

GIVEN `y` IS A `My year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 32D applies` IF
    `y`'s `I was a member of a couple throughout the period` AND `y`'s `my partner must lodge a tax return for the year`

GIVEN `y` IS A `My year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 32P applies` IF
        (NOT `y`'s `I was a member of a couple at some time in the period`)
    AND `y`'s `I was on income support throughout the period`
    AND (NOT `y`'s `I had maintenance income`)

@export Have I satisfied the FTB reconciliation conditions for the year (ss 32B-32D, 32J, 32P)?
GIVEN `my year` IS A `My year` @desc Your tax return, your partner's, any income support, and what you have notified
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I satisfied the FTB reconciliation conditions` IF
        (`s 32C applies` `my year` OR `s 32D applies` `my year` OR `my year`'s `someone whose income counts need not lodge` OR `s 32P applies` `my year`)
    AND ((NOT `s 32C applies` `my year`) OR (`my year`'s `I lodged my return in time` AND `my year`'s `my assessment has been made`))
    AND ((NOT `s 32D applies` `my year`) OR (`my year`'s `my partner lodged in time` AND `my year`'s `my partner's assessment has been made`))
    AND ((NOT `my year`'s `someone whose income counts need not lodge`) OR `my year`'s `I notified my income in time, or the Secretary can work it out`)
    AND ((NOT `s 32P applies` `my year`) OR `my year`'s `the income year has ended`)

-- s 32A(2) and s 105A(2)(f): the supplements are left out of my rate until the conditions are met, then taken into account.
@export Are the FTB Part A and Part B supplements included in my FTB yet (ss 32A, 105A)?
GIVEN `I have satisfied the reconciliation conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have satisfied the FTB reconciliation conditions for the year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my FTB supplements included yet` IF `I have satisfied the reconciliation conditions`

§§ `105, 105A, 71(2) -- what reconciliation gives me or takes back`

-- The year-end review is the Secretary's review under s 105 of the instalment determination (s 32AF(1)(b) describes it:
-- "on the basis of the individual's adjusted taxable income as finally determined"), forced by s 105A once the conditions
-- are met. If the correct amount on the final income is higher than what was paid, the review creates an entitlement and
-- the difference is paid (a top-up; s 107 sets its date of effect). If it is lower, s 71(2): "the difference between the
-- received amount and the correct amount is a debt due to the Commonwealth by the person". The correct amount includes the
-- supplements only if the conditions are met (s 32A). The FTB amounts are worked out under the Family Assistance Act
-- (fa-families.l4) and are inputs.
DECLARE `Reconciliation outcome` IS ONE OF
    `a top-up is paid to me`
    `I owe a debt`
    `no change`

GIVEN `my FTB for the year on my final income, without supplements` IS A NUMBER
      `the supplements on my final income` IS A NUMBER
      `I have satisfied the reconciliation conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the correct amount for the year` MEANS
    `my FTB for the year on my final income, without supplements`
    PLUS (IF `I have satisfied the reconciliation conditions` THEN `the supplements on my final income` ELSE 0)

@export What is the result of reconciling my FTB for the year (ss 105A, 71(2))?
GIVEN `what I was paid for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The FTB paid to you for the year on your estimate
      `my FTB for the year on my final income, without supplements` IS A NUMBER @desc FTB for the year on your adjusted taxable income as finally determined, leaving out the supplements
      `the supplements on my final income` IS A NUMBER @desc The FTB Part A and Part B supplements for the year on that income
      `I have satisfied the reconciliation conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have satisfied the FTB reconciliation conditions
GIVETH A `Reconciliation outcome`
`What is the result of reconciling my FTB` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `correct` GREATER THAN `what I was paid for the year` THEN `a top-up is paid to me`
           IF `correct` LESS THAN `what I was paid for the year`    THEN `I owe a debt`
           OTHERWISE `no change`
    WHERE
        `correct` MEANS `the correct amount for the year` `my FTB for the year on my final income, without supplements`
                                                          `the supplements on my final income`
                                                          `I have satisfied the reconciliation conditions`

@export How much is my reconciliation top-up (ss 105, 105A)?
GIVEN `what I was paid for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The FTB paid to you for the year on your estimate
      `my FTB for the year on my final income, without supplements` IS A NUMBER @desc FTB for the year on your final income, leaving out the supplements
      `the supplements on my final income` IS A NUMBER @desc The FTB Part A and Part B supplements for the year
      `I have satisfied the reconciliation conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have satisfied the FTB reconciliation conditions
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my reconciliation top-up` MEANS
    `the positive part of`
        (`the correct amount for the year` `my FTB for the year on my final income, without supplements`
                                           `the supplements on my final income`
                                           `I have satisfied the reconciliation conditions`
         MINUS `what I was paid for the year`)

@export How much do I owe after reconciliation (s 71(2))?
GIVEN `what I was paid for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The FTB paid to you for the year on your estimate
      `my FTB for the year on my final income, without supplements` IS A NUMBER @desc FTB for the year on your final income, leaving out the supplements
      `the supplements on my final income` IS A NUMBER @desc The FTB Part A and Part B supplements for the year
      `I have satisfied the reconciliation conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have satisfied the FTB reconciliation conditions
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much do I owe after reconciliation` MEANS
    `the positive part of`
        (`what I was paid for the year`
         MINUS `the correct amount for the year` `my FTB for the year on my final income, without supplements`
                                                 `the supplements on my final income`
                                                 `I have satisfied the reconciliation conditions`)

§§ `28, 28AA -- if a tax return is never lodged`

-- s 28(1)-(2): where the claimant was entitled to FTB for days in "the income year ... that began 2 years before the
-- beginning of the income year in which the particular time occurs", and the claimant or the partner "are required to
-- lodge an income tax return for the cancellation income year but have not done so by the particular time", and no
-- assessment has been made, "the Secretary must vary the determination so that ... the claimant is not, and never was,
-- entitled to family tax benefit for the cancellation days" -- and all of it becomes a debt (s 71(1)). s 28AA(1): the
-- individual "is taken not to have been entitled to" the newborn upfront payment for those days too. The cancellation
-- year is the current year less 2; once applied the variation stands until ss 28(3)-(6) undo it (not encoded), so a later
-- year is treated the same (INFERENCE).
@export Do I lose all my FTB for a year because a tax return for it was not lodged (s 28)?
GIVEN `the income year of my FTB` IS A NUMBER @desc The income year you were paid FTB for
      `the current income year` IS A NUMBER @desc The income year it is now
      `I or my partner must lodge and have not` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, or your partner then and now, were required to lodge a return for that year and have not
      `an assessment has been made for everyone who must lodge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the tax office has nonetheless assessed everyone who had to lodge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I lose my FTB for an unlodged return` IF
        `the current income year` AT LEAST `the income year of my FTB` PLUS 2
    AND `I or my partner must lodge and have not`
    AND (NOT `an assessment has been made for everyone who must lodge`)

@export Do I also lose the newborn upfront payment (s 28AA)?
GIVEN `I lost FTB for the year under s 28` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 28 has cancelled your FTB for the year
      `my newborn supplement days fall in that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the days your newborn supplement was added fall in the cancelled days
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I also lose the newborn upfront payment` IF
    `I lost FTB for the year under s 28` AND `my newborn supplement days fall in that year`

§§ `32AF -- after two years of over-estimating to a nil rate`

-- s 32AF(1)-(2): if in 2 consecutive income years the individual was paid FTB on an estimated income basis and, on review
-- against the income "as finally determined", the Part A rate was nil "because of the individual's adjusted taxable
-- income" in each year, the individual "is not entitled, on and after the exclusion day, to be paid the Part A rate of
-- family tax benefit worked out on an estimated income basis" ((3): 1 July after the later year). (b) the same for Part B
-- when nil under the $100,000 limit (Sch 1 cl 28B(1)). The parent can still claim for a past period after the year. The
-- exceptions -- a later year with a rate above nil (s 32AG), income support (s 32AI), a new FTB child (s 32AJ), separation
-- (s 32AK), special circumstances (s 32AL) -- are asked as one fact.
@export Am I barred from FTB Part A by instalment on an estimate after two nil years (s 32AF)?
GIVEN `my Part A was nil on final income in the earlier year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether reconciliation found your Part A nil because of income in the first of two consecutive years
      `my Part A was nil on final income in the later year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the same happened in the next year
      `an exception in ss 32AG-32AL applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a new FTB child, income support, a separation, a later year above nil, or special circumstances
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from Part A on an estimate` IF
        `my Part A was nil on final income in the earlier year`
    AND `my Part A was nil on final income in the later year`
    AND (NOT `an exception in ss 32AG-32AL applies`)

§§ `71, 77, 78, 78C, 78D, 93B -- my debt`

-- s 71(1): an amount paid "by way of family tax benefit" for a period for which "the person was not entitled" is a debt;
-- (2) the excess over "the correct amount" is a debt. s 77(1): the Secretary "must give the person a notice"; (2) "The
-- outstanding amount of the debt is due and payable on the 28th day after the date of the notice."
@export On which day after the date of the debt notice is my debt due (s 77(2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `On which day after the notice is my debt due` IS 28

-- s 78(1): interest charge accrues if an amount "remains unpaid at the end of the day ... on which the debt is due" and
-- "there is no arrangement in effect under section 91". s 78D(1): "not liable ... if on the day before the start of the
-- period ... (a) the person is receiving instalments of family tax benefit; or (b) ... a social security payment" (and
-- veterans', ABSTUDY living allowance, isolated children instalments, or a Minister's instrument). s 78E: the Secretary may
-- determine it is not payable. s 78A (a failed arrangement) is not encoded.
@export Must I pay interest charge on my FTB debt (ss 78, 78D, 78E)?
GIVEN `some of the debt is unpaid after the due day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any of the debt was still unpaid at the end of the 28th day
      `I have a repayment arrangement in effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a s 91 arrangement to repay by instalments was in effect at the end of that day
      `I was receiving FTB instalments or a social security payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the day before interest would start, you were receiving FTB instalments or a social security (or veterans', ABSTUDY living allowance or isolated children) payment
      `the Secretary has determined interest is not payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary has made a s 78E determination for you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I pay interest charge` IF
        `some of the debt is unpaid after the due day`
    AND (NOT `I have a repayment arrangement in effect`)
    AND (NOT `I was receiving FTB instalments or a social security payment`)
    AND (NOT `the Secretary has determined interest is not payable`)

-- s 78C(1): "the interest charge rate for a day is the rate worked out by adding 7 percentage points to the base interest
-- rate for that day, and dividing that total by the number of days in the calendar year". (2) the base rate is the RBA
-- monthly average yield of 90-day Bank Accepted Bills for a set month: an input. In percent.
@export What is the interest charge rate for a day, in percent (s 78C)?
GIVEN `the base interest rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The 90-day bank bill yield for the quarter, in percent
      `days in the calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc 365, or 366 in a leap year
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the interest charge rate for a day` MEANS
    (`the base interest rate` PLUS 7) DIVIDED BY `days in the calendar year`

-- s 93B: "legal proceedings, or any action under a provision of this Part, for the recovery of a debt may be commenced or
-- taken at any time". The years since the debt arose are read by nothing.
@export Can my FTB debt still be recovered after this many years (s 93B)?
GIVEN `years since the debt arose` IS A NUMBER @desc How long ago the debt arose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my debt still be recovered` IF TRUE

§§ `97, 99 -- must my debt be waived`

-- s 99(1): "The Secretary must waive the right to recover a debt if the debt is, or is likely to be, less than the amount
-- referred to in section 1237AAA of the Social Security Act 1991" (note 1: $250 immediately before 1 July 2026; indexed each
-- 1 July). That amount is in another Act: an input.
@export Must my debt be waived as a small debt (s 99)?
GIVEN `my debt` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of your debt
      `the small debt amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount in s 1237AAA of the Social Security Act 1991 for the year ($250 just before 1 July 2026)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my debt be waived as small` IF `my debt` LESS THAN `the small debt amount`

-- s 97(1): the Secretary "must waive" the "administrative error proportion" -- the part "attributable solely to an
-- administrative error made by the Commonwealth" -- if (2) "the debtor received in good faith the payment" and "would
-- suffer severe financial hardship if it were not waived"; or (3) the debt "is raised after the end of: (i) the debtor's
-- next income year after the one in which the eligibility period ... occurs; or (ii) the period of 13 weeks starting on the
-- day on which the payment ... was made; whichever ends last", and the payment was received in good faith. 13 weeks is 91
-- days, counted from the payment day as day 0 (INFERENCE about counting).
@export Must the administrative-error part of my debt be waived (s 97)?
GIVEN `the debt is solely the Commonwealth's administrative error` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether (this part of) the debt arose solely from an administrative error by the Commonwealth
      `I received the payment in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received the payment in good faith
      `I would suffer severe financial hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would suffer severe financial hardship if it were not waived
      `the income year of the payment period` IS A NUMBER @desc The income year of the period the payment was for
      `the income year the debt was raised` IS A NUMBER @desc The income year in which the debt was raised
      `days from the payment to the debt being raised` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the payment to the debt being raised
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the administrative error part be waived` IF
        `the debt is solely the Commonwealth's administrative error`
    AND `I received the payment in good faith`
    AND (   `I would suffer severe financial hardship`
         OR (    `the income year the debt was raised` GREATER THAN `the income year of the payment period` PLUS 1
             AND `days from the payment to the debt being raised` AT LEAST 91))

-- s 100(4): if the Secretary and the debtor agree that the debt "will be fully satisfied if the debtor pays ... an agreed
-- amount less than the amount of the debt outstanding at the time of the agreement (the unpaid amount), the Secretary must
-- waive the right to recover the difference". (5): the Secretary "must not make an agreement ... unless the Secretary is
-- satisfied that the agreed amount is at least the present value of the unpaid amount if it is repaid in instalments".
-- (6), transcribed (C2004A00491.formulas.md):
--     (Annual repayment / Interest) x [1 - 1 / (1 + Interest)^rp]
-- "annual repayment" is what the Secretary believes would be recovered in a year without the agreement; "interest" the
-- annual rate the Minister specifies by legislative instrument (not deposited: an input, as a fraction, 0.05 for 5%);
-- "rp" the years needed to repay the unpaid amount at the annual repayment. All three are inputs. Whether the Secretary
-- agrees at all is a fact.
@export What is the least I can agree to pay to settle my FTB debt in full (s 100(5), (6))?
GIVEN `the annual repayment` IS A NUMBER @desc What the Secretary believes would be recovered from you in a year without an agreement
      `the interest rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The annual interest rate the Minister specifies, as a fraction (0.05 for 5%)
      `the repayment period in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of years needed to repay the unpaid amount at the annual repayment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the present value of my unpaid debt` MEANS
    (`the annual repayment` DIVIDED BY `the interest rate`)
        TIMES (1 MINUS (1 DIVIDED BY ((1 PLUS `the interest rate`) EXPONENT `the repayment period in years`)))

@export How much of my FTB debt must be waived under a part-payment agreement (s 100(4), (5))?
GIVEN `the Secretary and I agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the Secretary agreed that paying the agreed amount satisfies the debt
      `the unpaid amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The debt outstanding when the agreement is made
      `the agreed amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you agree to pay
      `the present value of the unpaid amount` IS A NUMBER @desc Its present value under s 100(6) (see the question above)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my debt is waived on a part-payment agreement` MEANS
    IF     `the Secretary and I agreed`
       AND `the agreed amount` AT LEAST `the present value of the unpaid amount`
       AND `the agreed amount` LESS THAN `the unpaid amount`
    THEN `the unpaid amount` MINUS `the agreed amount`
    ELSE 0

§§ `108, 109D, 109E, 111A -- my review rights`

-- s 109A(1): "A person affected by a decision ... may apply to the Secretary for review". s 108(2)(e), (3): a determination
-- "to the extent the determination is based on an estimate of adjusted taxable income for an income year ... is not to be
-- reviewed under section 109A unless the applicant applies for the review after the end of the relevant income year and
-- ... (a) the Commissioner of Taxation has, on the basis of income tax returns lodged before the end of the income year
-- immediately after the relevant income year, made an assessment ... of all persons whose taxable income was relevant ...;
-- (b) there is no person whose taxable income was relevant ... who was required to lodge". (A determination refusing FTB
-- because the estimate is not reasonable, s 19 / s 28A, is reviewable at once: s 108(2)(e)(i).)
@export Can I ask for review of my FTB decision based on my income estimate yet (s 108(3))?
GIVEN `the decision is based on my income estimate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision rests on an estimate of adjusted taxable income (not a refusal of the estimate as unreasonable)
      `the income year has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the income year the estimate was for has ended
      `everyone relevant has been assessed on returns lodged in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the tax office has assessed everyone whose income counted, on returns lodged by the end of the next income year
      `nobody whose income counted had to lodge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether nobody whose income counted was required to lodge a return
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I ask for review of my estimate-based decision yet` IF
        (NOT `the decision is based on my income estimate`)
    OR  (    `the income year has ended`
         AND (`everyone relevant has been assessed on returns lodged in time` OR `nobody whose income counted had to lodge`))

-- s 109D(1): an application for review "of any decision (other than an excepted decision) must be made no later than: (a)
-- for a decision in relation to CCS or ACCS ...--90 days after the applicant is notified ...; and (b) otherwise--52 weeks".
-- (6) "excepted decision means a decision: (a) relating to the payment to a person of family tax benefit by instalment; or
-- (b) relating to the raising of a debt under Division 2 of Part 4". (3): a past-period decision for the income year of the
-- application or the year before can be reviewed even after 52 weeks. (2) the Secretary may extend for special
-- circumstances (not encoded). s 111A(1): ART review "no later than 90 days after the person is notified"; (5) the same two
-- kinds of decision are excepted and (4) have no time limit.
DECLARE `The kind of decision` IS ONE OF
    `a decision about my FTB by instalment`
    `a decision raising a debt`
    `a decision on my lump-sum claim for a past period`
    `another FTB decision`
    `a child care subsidy decision`

DECLARE `Review time limit` IS ONE OF
    `no time limit`
    `52 weeks after I am notified`
    `90 days after I am notified`

@export How long do I have to ask the Secretary to review a decision (s 109D)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The kind of decision` @desc What the decision is about
      `the past period is this income year or last` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a lump-sum claim decision, whether the period is in the income year you apply in or the year before
GIVETH A `Review time limit`
`How long do I have to ask for internal review` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a decision about my FTB by instalment`           THEN `no time limit`
    WHEN `a decision raising a debt`                       THEN `no time limit`
    WHEN `a decision on my lump-sum claim for a past period` THEN
        IF `the past period is this income year or last` THEN `no time limit` ELSE `52 weeks after I am notified`
    WHEN `another FTB decision`                            THEN `52 weeks after I am notified`
    WHEN `a child care subsidy decision`                   THEN `90 days after I am notified`

@export How long do I have to apply to the Administrative Review Tribunal (s 111A)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The kind of decision` @desc What the reviewed decision is about
GIVETH A `Review time limit`
`How long do I have to apply to the ART` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a decision about my FTB by instalment` THEN `no time limit`
    WHEN `a decision raising a debt`             THEN `no time limit`
    OTHERWISE `90 days after I am notified`

-- s 109E(1): if review of an instalment decision is applied for "more than 52 weeks after the person was given notice of the
-- original decision" and creates or increases entitlement, "the date of effect ... is the first day of the period to which
-- the original decision relates"; but (2AA) where that day is earlier than "the first day (the cut-off day) of the income
-- year before the income year in which the application ... was made", the person "cannot be paid any entitlement ... in
-- relation to any day earlier than the cut-off day". (2A) the cut-off does not apply where the person has satisfied the FTB
-- reconciliation conditions for the period (and the original decision was not itself a review decision). Within 52 weeks
-- s 109E does not limit backdating (INFERENCE: it does not apply). The special-circumstances extension (2) is not encoded.
@export From which income year can increased FTB be paid on my review (s 109E)?
GIVEN `weeks from the notice to my application` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks after you were notified of the original decision you applied for review
      `the income year the original decision's period starts in` IS A NUMBER @desc The income year in which the period covered by the original decision begins
      `the income year I apply in` IS A NUMBER @desc The income year in which you apply for review
      `I have satisfied the reconciliation conditions for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you satisfied the FTB reconciliation conditions for the period (s 109E(2A))
GIVETH A NUMBER
`From which income year can increased FTB be paid` MEANS
    IF     `weeks from the notice to my application` GREATER THAN 52
       AND (NOT `I have satisfied the reconciliation conditions for the period`)
    THEN max `the income year the original decision's period starts in` (`the income year I apply in` MINUS 1)
    ELSE `the income year the original decision's period starts in`
